  "body": "Reported by the maintainer in chat, 2026-11-16:\n\n> \"while generating a toolpath a \"progress\" bar should overlay the view port.\"\n\nWhat happens: while an operation generates its toolpath, the viewport shows no progress. The user cannot see that the work runs, how far it is, or which operation it is.\n\nExpected: while one or more generate jobs run, a progress bar lies over the viewport.\n\n- It names the operation that generates.\n- It shows the progress. Where the generator reports no fraction, it shows an activity bar and the elapsed time.\n- It goes away when the job ends, is refused or is cancelled. A refusal still shows its message as it does today.\n- With more than one job, it shows the count (\"2 of 5\") and the current operation.\n- The text is plain English, with no G-code terms.\n\nRules:\n\n- The bar is ephemeral UI state: it is not a command and it is not in the undo history.\n- It reads the state of the generate jobs. It starts no work and it does not block the UI thread.\n- It obeys the frame cost rule of #2238: an unchanged frame does no work in proportion to the model, and the bar requests a repaint only while a job runs.\n- It changes no toolpath and no posted G-code.\n\nDone means: a structural test (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/structural.rs` family) pins that the bar is present with the operation name while a job runs and is absent after the job ends or is refused; the PR has before and after screenshots.\n",
